# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  API keys — fill in, then run ./sv doctor
#
#  1. `./sv setup` copies this file to config/secrets.env (or: cp config/secrets.example.env config/secrets.env)
#  2. Paste each key after its "=" — no quotes, no spaces.
#  3. `./sv doctor` shows ✓ for every key it found. Keys are never printed, logged or committed
#     (config/secrets.env is git-ignored). All services below have a free tier; nothing here is paid.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── REQUIRED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Narration: Google Gemini text-to-speech (30 voices, performance tags, free tier).
#   Get it: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey → "Create API key".
#   Without it: record your own voice and use ./sv voice-import <slug> file.wav.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── RECOMMENDED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Photos + vertical b-roll video clips — the biggest source of modern / atmospheric images.
#   Get it: https://www.pexels.com/api/ → "Get started" (instant, free).
PEXELS_API_KEY=

# Sound effects search (CC0 sounds) when the built-in bank lacks a sound (./sv sfx fetch).
#   Get it: https://freesound.org/apiv2/apply → create an app, copy the "Client secret/Api key".
#   Without it: sounds are searched through Openverse (no key needed), with fewer results.
FREESOUND_API_KEY=

# ── OPTIONAL (more image sources) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pixabay photos + videos:            https://pixabay.com/api/docs/ (log in, the key is on that page)
PIXABAY_API_KEY=
# Unsplash photos (the "Access Key"):  https://unsplash.com/developers → New Application
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=
# Smithsonian Open Access (museum objects, CC0). Works without a key (shared DEMO_KEY, rate-limited):
#   https://api.data.gov/signup/
SMITHSONIAN_API_KEY=

# No key needed: Wikimedia Commons, Openverse, The Met, Cleveland Museum of Art, Art Institute of Chicago.
# Image generation needs no key either: an agent with its own image tool (e.g. Codex $imagegen) generates
# images itself (skills/05-image-sourcing §4); this studio never calls an image API.
